.TH START-NOVNC-CONNECTION.SH 1 "2026-10-29" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-novnc-connection.sh \- open a tunnel to the noVNC manager and browse a session dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-novnc-connection.sh
[\fB\-H\fR \fIhost\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-J\fR \fIproxy_jump\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIlocal_port\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIremote_port\fR]
[\fB\-P\fR \fIpassword_file\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIsessions_file\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-native\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBClient side.\fR Run this on your own laptop or workstation, after
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1)
has set up the ssh paths and recorded your username as \fBNOVNC_USER\fR.
.PP
.B start-novnc-connection.sh
opens an SSH tunnel from a free local port to port 443 (by default) on
the noVNC manager host, logged in as the current user unless
overridden. Once the tunnel is accepting connections, the plain
session-list page normally served at \fBhttps://localhost:\fIlocal_port\fR
is fetched and scraped, and its links are rendered into a
self-contained, modern-looking "dashboard" HTML page with one card per
VNC session. That generated page, not the raw session list, is what
gets opened in the browser.
.PP
If a VNC password file is found (see \fB\-P\fR below), each card's link
is built with noVNC's \fBpassword\fR and \fBautoconnect=true\fR query
parameters so the session connects automatically instead of prompting
for a password.
.PP
Each card shows the session's login account, the host it runs on
(with the X display number when known) and a description of what the
desktop is for. Descriptions and card order come from
.BR novnc-sessions.yaml (5)
(see \fB\-c\fR below). Cards follow that file's order, then any
sessions the portal offers but the file does not name, in the portal's
order. Reading the file needs PyYAML in the \fBpython3\fR on your
\fBPATH\fR; without it, or without the file, the cards appear in portal
order with no descriptions and one warning says why.
.PP
For every session the sessions file gives a \fBdisplay\fR for, and that
runs on the tunnel host, the same ssh also forwards a free local port to
the session's VNC port, 5900+\fIdisplay\fR. Its card then offers
\fBNative VNC\fR, a \fBvnc://localhost:\fIport\fR link that macOS opens in
Screen Sharing, and shows the forward and the equivalent
\fBopen vnc://localhost:\fIport\fR command. The viewer asks for the
session's VNC password itself. A session whose host differs from the
session on another host gets its native forward through a separate ssh
to that host, because Xvnc listens only on its own host's loopback; the
tunnel panel lists each such ssh with its pid and command. Cards are
arranged in the labeled groups of
.BR novnc-sessions.yaml (5),
with a separator between groups.
.PP
A panel at the top of the page describes the tunnel: ssh user and host,
jump host, ssh pid, the portal forward, the number of native forwards,
and the complete equivalent \fBssh\fR command. The forwards exist only
while the script runs.
.PP
The tunnel, and the temporary directory holding the generated
dashboard file, are torn down when the script exits, whether via
Ctrl-C, the ssh session dying, or normal termination.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default. The .env tier is read only when
.BR daq-common.sh (3)
is installed alongside this script; without it the script still runs,
from the environment and defaults alone.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Remote host to tunnel to. Environment: \fBNOVNC_HOST\fR. Default:
\fImu2e\-mgr\-01.fnal.gov\fR.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
SSH user. Environment: \fBNOVNC_USER\fR. Default: the current user.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-proxy\-jump " " \fIHOST\fR
SSH ProxyJump host used to reach the remote host (passed to
.BR ssh (1)
as \fB\-J\fR). The special value \fBnone\fR (or an empty string)
disables the jump host. Environment: \fBNOVNC_PROXY_JUMP\fR. Default:
\fImu2egateway01.fnal.gov\fR when the remote host is
\fImu2e\-mgr\-01.fnal.gov\fR, otherwise no jump host is used.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Local port for the tunnel. Environment: \fBNOVNC_LOCAL_PORT\fR.
Default: an automatically chosen free port.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Remote port to forward to. Environment: \fBNOVNC_REMOTE_PORT\fR.
Default: \fI443\fR.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to a file whose first line is the VNC password. When present,
it is used to build auto-connecting session links. Environment:
\fBNOVNC_PASSWORD_FILE\fR. Default: \fI~/.novnc_password\fR; if the
file does not exist, links are generated without a password and
without auto-connect. If the file is readable by group or other, a
warning is printed recommending \fBchmod 600\fR, but the password is
still used.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sessions " " \fIFILE\fR
YAML file of session descriptions and card order; see
.BR novnc-sessions.yaml (5).
Environment: \fBNOVNC_SESSIONS_FILE\fR. An explicit file must exist.
Default: \fBnovnc-sessions.yaml\fR on the toolkit's config search path
(\fI./config\fR, the checkout's \fIconfig/\fR,
\fI~/.config/mu2edaq\fR, \fI/etc/mu2edaq\fR), ignored if none is found.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-native
Do not add the native VNC forwards; cards show no native link.
Environment: \fBNOVNC_NATIVE\fR=\fB0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the ssh command (with every forward), target URL, sessions file
and native links that would be used, and exit
without opening a tunnel or a browser.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BROWSER
If set, used to launch the dashboard page. Falls back to
.BR xdg-open (1)
on Linux, or
.BR open (1)
on macOS.
.TP
.B NOVNC_HOST ", " NOVNC_USER ", " NOVNC_PROXY_JUMP ", " NOVNC_LOCAL_PORT ", " NOVNC_REMOTE_PORT ", " NOVNC_PASSWORD_FILE ", " NOVNC_SESSIONS_FILE ", " NOVNC_NATIVE
See OPTIONS above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.novnc_password
Default location for the VNC password used to build auto-connecting
session links. Should be readable only by the owner
(\fBchmod 600\fR).
.TP
.I config/novnc-sessions.yaml
Shipped session descriptions and card order. A personal copy in
\fI~/.config/mu2edaq/novnc-sessions.yaml\fR is used when no
\fIconfig/\fR directory earlier on the search path has one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The dry run or help completed.
.TP
.B 1
An option was not recognised, the \fB\-c\fR file does not exist, no
free local port could be found, or
\fBssh\fR exited before the tunnel came up.
.PP
Otherwise the script waits on the tunnel and returns the exit status
of \fBssh\fR when it closes; an interrupt with Ctrl-C tears the tunnel
down and exits with the shell's interrupt status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open a tunnel with all defaults:
.PP
.RS
.EX
start-novnc-connection.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview the ssh command without connecting:
.PP
.RS
.EX
start-novnc-connection.sh --dry-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable auto-connecting session links:
.PP
.RS
.EX
echo "mypassword" > ~/.novnc_password
chmod 600 ~/.novnc_password
start-novnc-connection.sh
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR novnc-sessions.yaml (5),
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1),
.BR daq\-ssh\-check.sh (1),
.BR manage-vnc-servers.sh (1),
.BR ssh (1)
